# Programs in the FUZIX test corpus that are NOT identical to their
# .expected files when run with a display (tests/sweep/run-corpus.sh).
# Four are the files' own limitation: the .expected was blessed on a
# host with no display and no sound, and with a server the program
# reads something real - mminfo's lock state, printat's cursor escapes,
# and the one legitimate PLAY SOUND in play and strargs, which the
# goldens expect to fail with "Sound output did not start" and which
# now plays.  Ten are the pin and peripheral tests, which a PC refuses
# until phase 8.  A name leaving this list is progress; a name arriving
# is a fault.
mminfo
printat
play
strargs
countpin
gpio
i2c2
pinint
pioout
port
pulse
pulsin
pwm
waitint
